# Shell scripts run on macOS and are shipped to it verbatim by scp, so a CRLF
# working tree breaks them at the shebang: `/bin/zsh` is not a file that
# exists, and the error blames the interpreter rather than the line ending.
# Observed exactly that way after a Python rewrite of deploy/*.sh on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.plist text eol=lf
